title: Family
---

Parent: The train is almost here, okay? Do you have everything? 
Parent: Pencils, pens, lunch? I packed your favorite snack, grapes and apple slices.
Child: Thank you mommy!
Parent: Are you excited for your first day of fifth grade?
Child: Yeah, I'm in the same class as Angelina! 
Parent: That's great, sweetie. Tell their mom I say hello, ok?
Child: But James is in my class, too. He laughed at me and said I'm too short. 
Child: And last year he pushed me outside at recess and my tooth fell out.
Parent: I'm sorry, sweetie. But, there have been three months of summer. 
Parent: Hopefully James has reflected on his behavior and now he's a little more mature.
Parent: But if he doesn't, tell the teacher or the counselor. And tell me too. 
Parent: I'll have a nice chat with his father.
Child: Ok, mommy!


===

