title: Employees
---
<<if $ratseen is true>>
<<jump Employees_SeeRat>>
<<endif>>

Employee 1: It's definitely the 1.
Employee 2: Nah, it's the G.
Employee 1: I've never been assigned to the G, so I wouldn't know.
Employee 2: I'll tell you which line is not the best. The A for sure.
Employee 1: Yeah, of course. It's forced to stop every 5 minutes. And they never let us make the announcements. It's always that stupid robot voice.
Employee 2: I mean, I like getting a break from announcing. But hearing it again and again is so annoying.
Employee 1: It's like Siri and Alexa mashed together in the worst way.
Employee 2: But the A line does have the newer trains. 
Employee 1: Yeah, and they stop more! What's up with that? Shouldn't new be more efficient?
Employee 1: That's why I like the 1. Older cars, but it's dependable. And it's got personality.
Employee 2: Some crazy shit happens on the 1 though. One time I saw a guy clip his toenails and eat them.
Employee 1: …
Employee 1: Thanks for ruining my day, bro.

===

