title: Students
---
<<if $ratseen is true>>
<<jump Students_SeeRat>>
<<endif>>

Student 1: He yelled at me.
Student 2: What?!?
Student 1: Yeah, and in front of the whole class too. 
Student 2: Why?? 
Student 3: That's so crazy for a professor to do. 
Student 1: Right… And it wasn't even for anything serious. He asked us which article of the National General law granted permission for the judicial branch to pass judgement on the status of civil lawsuits and I said Article 29 instead of Article 28.
Student 3: Oh my god. 
Student 1: He said the time, energy, and finances of the Law School and its professors are being wasted on simpletons like me.
Student 2: That's messed up, man.
Student 1: Yeah, but he's tenured, so it's impossible to get him fired. 
Student 2: This is Professor Draconian, right?
Student 1: Yeah.
Student 3: He got his law degree like 10 billion years ago. Does he get off on putting his students down?
Student 2: Ew, don't put that image in my head.
Student 3: Getting tenure is such a scam. At this point, all we can do is wait for him to croak.

===

